{{- /*
  github/shared/pr-rebase-if-behind — rebase a PR branch onto its base in a
  temporary worktree, force-push with --force-with-lease on success, or
  notify (and optionally spawn a rebase-conflict child) on failure.

  Callers: babysit-this-pr §3a, babysit-my-prs §3a.

  Placeholders substituted by the agent from the surrounding context:
    <number>       — the PR number
    <owner>/<repo> — the target repository
    <headRefName>  — the PR's branch
    <baseRefName>  — the PR's base branch
    <title>        — the PR title

  Interaction mode: callers already established interactive vs silent mode.
  This fragment refers to that mode in shorthand.
*/ -}}
Check whether the PR branch is behind its base and cannot cleanly merge:

```bash
gh pr view <number> --repo <owner>/<repo> --json mergeStateStatus,mergeable,baseRefName,headRefName
```

If the PR is behind and needs a rebase:

- **Interactive mode**: ask before rebasing (offer "Yes, rebase", "Skip",
  "Spawn a conversation to handle it").
- **Silent mode**: `mitto_ui_notify` (`info`) that a rebase is starting and
  proceed automatically.

Do the rebase inside a **temporary worktree** — never mutate the user's main
checkout. Run the git commands inside a local checkout of `<owner>/<repo>`
(the current folder if it is that repo, otherwise the temp clone from
Step 1):

```bash
git fetch origin <baseRefName> <headRefName>
TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)
git worktree add "$TMPDIR" origin/<headRefName> --detach
cd "$TMPDIR" && git rebase origin/<baseRefName>
```

**On conflicts**:

```bash
git rebase --abort
cd - && git worktree remove "$TMPDIR" --force
```

Then `mitto_ui_notify` (`warning`, `sound: true`, `native: true`) that manual
rebase is needed. If `mitto_conversation_new` is available and no dedup match
exists, spawn a one-off rebase-conflict child:

```
mitto_conversation_new(self_id: "{{ .Session.ID }}",
  title: "Rebase PR #<number>: <title>",
  initial_prompt: "PR #<number> (<title>) in <owner>/<repo> needs rebasing onto <baseRefName> but has conflicts.
    Check out branch <headRefName>, rebase onto origin/<baseRefName>,
    resolve the conflicts, and force-push with --force-with-lease.
    Never touch the main checkout at <repo path> — use a fresh worktree.",
  acp_server: <prefer "coding" or "fast" tagged server>)
```

Then skip to the next step (or the next PR in a multi-PR loop).

**On success**:

```bash
git push --force-with-lease origin HEAD:refs/heads/<headRefName>
cd - && git worktree remove "$TMPDIR" --force
```

Then `mitto_ui_notify` (`success`) that the PR was rebased.

If the PR is already up-to-date on its base, this step is **not actionable**.
